{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now do not be grieved, etc.</b> One needs to know why it says ״וְעַתָּה״ — what does the word come to remove? Second, why did he repeat, saying <b>do not be grieved and let it not kindle</b> — and moreover they are two opposite things: grief (עִצָּבוֹן) indicates a broken heart, while anger (חֲרוֹן אַף) indicates pride. Further, one needs to know why he was precise in saying the word <b>hennah</b>?" "<b>Indeed,</b> the explanation of the matter is as follows: I know that you are grieved over the sale, as they revealed their mind in saying (Genesis 42:21) ״אֲבָל אֲשֵׁמִים אֲנַחְנוּ״, and also according to the midrash (Genesis Rabbah 91:3) that said they went down to ransom him with dear blood — therefore he said to them <b>and now</b>, meaning: since what they sought is now available to them through this revelation, they would remove the grief. And he also intended thereby to hint to them and inform them that he knows about them that their mind is close to him and they are grieved over him until now, and thereby he would justify that his heart is whole with them." "And his saying <b>let it not kindle in your eyes</b> means: because you sold me hennah — for you brought upon yourselves all the chain of events, the acts of bowing that for their sake you plotted to sell, as it is written (Genesis 37:20) ״וְנִרְאֶה מַה יִּהְיוּ״ etc. — and this thing would provoke anger, like a person who comes to set something right and finds himself causing harm, and his anger burns over what he brought upon himself. And he gave a reason for this: for on the contrary, their deeds brought them great good — ״for Elohim sent me before you to preserve life,״ ״for this, etc., to make for you a remnant״ etc. — and from now on it will not kindle in your eyes over the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:48.907879709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}